<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka to slash corporate profit tax to 30 pct.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka to slash corporate profit tax to 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka plans to slash corporate profit tax to 30 pct from 35 pct from April 1998, Deputy Finance Minister Gamini Lakshman Peiris said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The government will also remove the 0.5 percent stamp duty on share transactions to help the market to consolidate its recovery, Peiris told parliament as he presented the state budget for calendar 1997.</p>
<p>Peiris also said the governmment plans to make all listed company dividends tax free in the hands of shareholders to encourage companies to go public.</p>
</text>
